  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WFP integrated food security programme in Akobo, Uror and Nyirol Counties</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is for General Food Distribution (GFD) and Blanket Supplementary Feeding Programme (BSFP) Complementary Feeding. It aimed at Saving lives and providing nutrition -sensitive food assistance to crisis -affected population of Nyirol, Uror, Akobo East and West County in Jonglei State. This project is targeting 329,946 vulnerable individuals (Men, Boys, Women and girls) in Akobo, Uror, and Nyirol Counties, Jonglei State, South Sudan. Key interventions include: &#x2022; Emergency Food Assistance: Providing immediate relief through General Food Distribution (GFD) and Blanket Supplementary Feeding (BSF) to save lives and prevent malnutrition. &#x2022; Building Resilience: Empowering 3,600 beneficiaries to recover through GFD++ and livelihoods activities, including seed distribution and training. &#x2022; Improving Education and Nutrition: Enhancing school enrolment, attendance, and gender equity for 15,000 students in 21 targeted schools through daily hot school meals.</narrative>
  </description>
